WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:01.730
Hello the internet.

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:02.750
Am in a hole?

00:00:02.750 --> 00:00:04.200
I look like I'm shorter.

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:05.060
You're always shorter than me.

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:05.893
I'm always shorter.

00:00:05.893 --> 00:00:06.870
I'm Gav.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.703
I'm Dan.

00:00:07.703 --> 00:00:08.720
We're The Slow Mo Guys,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.660
I almost couldn't remember the name

00:00:09.660 --> 00:00:11.750
of our channel for a second.

00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.600
There's this company called SOG,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.270
or S-O-G, I'm not sure how they say it.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:17.103
They were like,

00:00:17.103 --> 00:00:18.370
"Hey, if we send you knives do you want

00:00:18.370 --> 00:00:19.780
to try and cut a bullet off with one?"

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:20.848
and I thought, yeah.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.007
Yeah.

00:00:23.007 --> 00:00:25.740
Just reply, yes.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:26.990
Yes, here's my address.

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:28.770
We're not going to use a real bullet,

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.116
we're just going to use
our trusty air pistol

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:32.980
because it's way less dangerous

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:34.730
and I have a very small backyard

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:38.470
where discharging a
firearm would be insanity.

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:40.830
You know we've got a
small back board here.

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:42.770
I think a bullet would
probably go through that.

00:00:42.770 --> 00:00:45.240
So we're going to try to cut the pellet,

00:00:45.240 --> 00:00:46.240
pop these two balloons.

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.388
Reminds me of one of
those 22plinkster videos,

00:00:48.388 --> 00:00:50.035
except you're not going to do it

00:00:50.035 --> 00:00:51.330
over your shoulder like this.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.650
I'm not going to be like
here firing stuff all over,

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.530
I'm just going to be like
right next to the thing

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:56.720
missing it all the time.

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.650
We're going to use the 2511 on this one.

00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.622
Need a fast camera,

00:00:59.622 --> 00:01:01.160
need a higher frame rate.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.020
Let's see what happens shall we?

00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:03.853
We'll start off by shooting this

00:01:03.853 --> 00:01:07.220
in a 28,000 fringe a second in 720p.

00:01:07.220 --> 00:01:09.290
And that means the use of the V2511,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.266
which is very loud.

00:01:12.951 --> 00:01:13.784
There it is.

00:01:13.784 --> 00:01:14.617
What?

00:01:14.617 --> 00:01:16.283
What?

00:01:16.283 --> 00:01:17.300
I can't hear you, what?

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:20.020
Okay what's your predictions
for how this first shot

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.170
is going to go?

00:01:21.170 --> 00:01:22.483
As this the first shot,

00:01:24.352 --> 00:01:25.756
I might need to get my eye in.

00:01:25.756 --> 00:01:27.050
Hone it in?

00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:29.610
Yeah remember the candle video we did?

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.443
Yeah.

00:01:30.443 --> 00:01:31.400
It took a few goes didn't it?

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:32.540
It did.

00:01:32.540 --> 00:01:34.650
So I'm thinking this is
going to be something similar

00:01:34.650 --> 00:01:35.800
where we have to get it

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:39.330
perfect on the left or right,

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.890
but it doesn't matter if
we get it not so perfect

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:41.884
on the up and down.

00:01:41.884 --> 00:01:43.831
All right I can get on board with that.

00:01:43.831 --> 00:01:45.343
All right I'm going to go.

00:01:45.343 --> 00:01:46.930
Have you got your eye protection on?

00:01:46.930 --> 00:01:47.763
What?

00:01:47.763 --> 00:01:48.596
Eye-pro?

00:01:48.596 --> 00:01:49.429
Yeah.

00:01:50.334 --> 00:01:51.167
Wow!

00:01:53.660 --> 00:01:54.500
I got hit.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.333
Did you?

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:56.380
What with?

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:57.213
Was it a shot?

00:01:57.213 --> 00:01:58.300
I don't know, something hit me.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.133
You all right?

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:00.115
Yeah.

00:02:00.115 --> 00:02:02.586
I don't know if it was balloon or not.

00:02:02.586 --> 00:02:03.940
Bugger.

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:04.864
It was the pellet.

00:02:04.864 --> 00:02:06.364
Just a tiny piece of pellet.

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:09.160
Wonder if it was this bouncing back.

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:10.343
It's not very safe is it?

00:02:11.527 --> 00:02:15.290
Lovely split, not really a 50/50 split,

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:18.568
but is it two pieces on that one side?

00:02:18.568 --> 00:02:19.700
Yeah.

00:02:19.700 --> 00:02:20.760
So it split into three?

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.660
Yeah I think so.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:26.160
Popped both balloons,

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:27.670
you see there it's hit the...

00:02:27.670 --> 00:02:29.550
Yeah it's coming right back at us.

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:30.383
How's that, wait?

00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:32.610
It's made a little chip in the wood,

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.050
and it's now just hurdling
back towards my hands.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:38.260
That looked like it was
going almost into the lens.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:39.510
Good job it didn't.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.500
Yeah.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:42.790
I mean, it hit my hand and
it didn't hurt that much,

00:02:42.790 --> 00:02:46.340
so it probably would've
just dinged the glass,

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.640
but still we need to
rethink our angles here.

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:50.930
Maybe it's just because
the angle of the back stop

00:02:50.930 --> 00:02:52.980
perfectly hit it and came back.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.170
What are the chances of that though?

00:02:54.170 --> 00:02:55.473
It could have gone anywhere.

00:02:55.473 --> 00:02:57.450
Damn good job we were
wearing eye protection.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.850
I did say, "You got
your eye protection on?"

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.195
It went right over your head.

00:03:00.195 --> 00:03:01.028
Yeah.

00:03:06.491 --> 00:03:08.157
Oh--

00:03:08.157 --> 00:03:08.990
You all right there?

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:09.823
No.

00:03:09.823 --> 00:03:10.656
Why what's going on?

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:12.862
The balloon is like weak at the rim

00:03:12.862 --> 00:03:13.710
so it's not like,

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:16.320
you know when you blow into
one normally it holds the rim

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.310
and lets you blow into it?

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:19.167
It's weak so I'm like--

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.700
It's not letting me blow into it.

00:03:21.700 --> 00:03:23.130
To avoid the same thing happening again

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:25.170
where it obviously hit the wood there

00:03:25.170 --> 00:03:26.480
and bounced straight back in the camera,

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.230
I'm going to try tilting the wood back

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:31.770
because of the angle
it's going to go higher.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:32.603
Sounds good.

00:03:32.603 --> 00:03:33.610
Miss the camera.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:35.510
Do you want a whole face protection?

00:03:36.450 --> 00:03:38.120
Yeah all right I'll go get one.

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:39.460
Good idea.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.700
I've changed the resolution to 512x320

00:03:41.700 --> 00:03:43.060
which is teenie weenie,

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:45.584
but we are now at 120,000 frames a second

00:03:45.584 --> 00:03:47.550
and I've got a nice, long treenie cable

00:03:47.550 --> 00:03:49.503
so I don't get hit again.

00:03:55.125 --> 00:03:56.167
I think I missed.

00:03:56.167 --> 00:03:58.223
Did you miss the knife?

00:03:58.223 --> 00:04:01.350
No I think I hit the side of the knife

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:03.870
and it deflected to the
left and hit the balloon.

00:04:03.870 --> 00:04:05.270
Oh all right.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:06.103
Oh no.

00:04:06.103 --> 00:04:06.936
Oh you actually got it.

00:04:06.936 --> 00:04:08.090
I did get it.

00:04:08.090 --> 00:04:10.223
Oh perfectly, baby.

00:04:10.223 --> 00:04:11.633
That was perfect.

00:04:15.251 --> 00:04:17.620
So I think the fault
was just in the angle.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.287
The actual shot on the knife--

00:04:20.550 --> 00:04:21.820
Oh it's satisfying.

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:23.574
That's perfect as well.

00:04:23.574 --> 00:04:25.112
Where did it go?

00:04:25.112 --> 00:04:27.100
So it went into the purple one,

00:04:27.100 --> 00:04:28.718
didn't pop, it went straight through,

00:04:28.718 --> 00:04:30.790
and I think it just missed the green one.

00:04:30.790 --> 00:04:31.623
What?

00:04:31.623 --> 00:04:34.173
Came out the other side of
the purple one, ripping it.

00:04:36.430 --> 00:04:37.410
Wow

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:38.243
Oh man.

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:42.070
It must have missed by such a fine amount

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.070
on that green there.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.410
Yeah, very close.

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:48.470
All right let's reset.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:49.303
Okay.

00:04:50.160 --> 00:04:51.910
You know, looking at the footage,

00:04:53.150 --> 00:04:55.330
it was like it was almost touching it.

00:04:55.330 --> 00:04:57.580
I feel like it looked like
it went directly into it

00:04:57.580 --> 00:04:58.510
and just disappeared.

00:04:58.510 --> 00:05:01.700
It must have just slightly...

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.890
Is that from it?

00:05:02.890 --> 00:05:05.800
No, maybe?

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.560
Do you think that it
could be from a scrape?

00:05:08.560 --> 00:05:09.440
That could be you know,

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:10.827
so see if we traced that,

00:05:10.827 --> 00:05:14.110
I can just about see the
knife from this position here.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:15.520
So it must have just scraped it there.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:17.133
It just goes past there.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:21.340
That's so close.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:22.530
Just for some curiosity here

00:05:22.530 --> 00:05:23.920
I've know switched the focus

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:25.560
from being on the front of the blade

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:27.840
to it's now the front of the balloons

00:05:27.840 --> 00:05:30.300
because we've seen what happens
when it splits on the blade,

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:32.010
so now we're really just interested

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.370
in seeing what happens at this point.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:34.350
Because on this balloon,

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:37.730
it went in and then popped
the other side of the balloon.

00:05:37.730 --> 00:05:39.263
It didn't split from the hole.

00:05:40.320 --> 00:05:41.153
It's so weird.

00:05:41.153 --> 00:05:41.986
Yeah.

00:05:45.846 --> 00:05:46.993
What happened?

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:49.540
Even though it missed that one

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:50.510
what was cool to see about that one

00:05:50.510 --> 00:05:53.640
is that you saw the pellet
go through the front,

00:05:53.640 --> 00:05:56.150
carry on through the
middle of the balloon,

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.400
and it still had enough speed

00:05:57.400 --> 00:05:58.670
and there was still enough tension

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.010
in the back of the balloon,

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:01.600
that it split through the back too.

00:06:01.600 --> 00:06:04.020
So it didn't just get caught
up in the loose rubber,

00:06:04.020 --> 00:06:05.350
it was still going fast enough

00:06:05.350 --> 00:06:07.410
and this was still stretched
enough for it just to go

00:06:07.410 --> 00:06:08.243
see you later.

00:06:08.243 --> 00:06:09.760
That really puts it into perspective

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.150
how quickly those pellets go.

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:13.580
Yeah.

00:06:13.580 --> 00:06:15.560
So by the time it hit
the back of the balloon,

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:17.360
half of the balloon was all ready open,

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:18.810
and it was just pretty much air on air.

00:06:18.810 --> 00:06:20.653
Even though the entry was that big

00:06:20.653 --> 00:06:23.680
and it still managed to
split at the other side.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.580
That's ridiculous.

00:06:25.770 --> 00:06:27.520
It can race through a balloon

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:29.120
quicker than the ballon can pop.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:31.133
It's fast.

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:31.966
That is fast.

00:06:31.966 --> 00:06:33.340
If it was a bullet it'd be even faster.

00:06:33.340 --> 00:06:35.486
Because I'm firing
directly down the blade,

00:06:35.486 --> 00:06:37.337
it's incredibly difficult to actually see

00:06:37.337 --> 00:06:39.193
where the the middle is,

00:06:40.110 --> 00:06:41.520
if not impossible.

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:42.353
Because it's so thin.

00:06:42.353 --> 00:06:43.390
Because it's so thin.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.090
So if you look directly at
the middle of the blade,

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.380
you see that?

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.590
Only one side should be purple

00:06:48.590 --> 00:06:49.950
then this side should be purple.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:50.795
Yeah.

00:06:50.795 --> 00:06:51.628
See that?

00:06:51.628 --> 00:06:53.450
That's why I'm using two different colors

00:06:53.450 --> 00:06:55.600
so that I can actually see
the middle of the blade

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:57.017
because other wise I'm basically like,

00:06:57.017 --> 00:07:00.450
"Right, directly in between
the yellow and the purple."

00:07:00.450 --> 00:07:01.740
Because other wise it
would just all be purple,

00:07:01.740 --> 00:07:02.577
I'd be like,

00:07:02.577 --> 00:07:05.960
"I don't know what--"

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:13.013
Wow amazing split again.

00:07:15.140 --> 00:07:18.770
Oh simultaneous, it's like
identical on both sides.

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:19.603
Perfect symmetry there.

00:07:19.603 --> 00:07:21.870
That's a lovely shot.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.475
Thank you, and well done for your shot.

00:07:24.475 --> 00:07:26.640
Thank you, Daniel.

00:07:26.640 --> 00:07:28.480
We will now get a side on angle

00:07:28.480 --> 00:07:29.830
with the green and the yellow.

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:30.690
How about that?

00:07:30.690 --> 00:07:32.480
Oh, how about that?

00:07:36.674 --> 00:07:37.590
What?

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:39.140
Surprised me for some reason.

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:41.053
No idea why.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.610
It surprised you?

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:45.519
Yeah.

00:07:45.519 --> 00:07:47.030
Shooting up ballons?

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:48.040
Bloody hell!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:48.873
It was loud.

00:08:13.490 --> 00:08:14.910
So I've managed to after looking

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:18.530
find half of the pellet I fired.

00:08:18.530 --> 00:08:20.790
So it's been completely
split in half by the knife.

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:22.070
As you can see,

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.760
the outside of it is
kind of dull and rusty

00:08:24.760 --> 00:08:28.800
because I let it get wet and
didn't really look after it.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:30.770
But if I turn it over,

00:08:30.770 --> 00:08:32.880
it's completely shiny and new.

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.300
The internal metal.

00:08:34.300 --> 00:08:37.150
And it's just been perfectly sliced.

00:08:37.150 --> 00:08:39.730
Some nice, very slow shweeny
looking footch there.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:40.620
Bit of metal on metal.

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:43.290
Satisfying how it just
perfectly sliced it in half.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.123
Yeah.

00:08:44.123 --> 00:08:45.230
It's not even managed to dent the knife,

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.360
it just sort of stained it.

00:08:46.360 --> 00:08:48.610
I think the pellet's just really soft.

00:08:48.610 --> 00:08:50.500
Yeah I'm sure if you hit
the pellets against anything

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:51.780
it would mush and split apart,

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:53.380
but because it's such a sharp knife

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.340
it's making very clean cuts through it

00:08:55.340 --> 00:08:57.470
and leaving you with that
polished edge on the inside.

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:00.560
It's even making the pellets
not perfectly straight,

00:09:00.560 --> 00:09:02.320
but the inside's been cut is like,

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:03.153
sort of concave like that

00:09:03.153 --> 00:09:05.310
because it's going like
that around the knife,

00:09:05.310 --> 00:09:06.580
and then being sent either direction

00:09:06.580 --> 00:09:08.263
so it's sort of going...

00:09:08.263 --> 00:09:09.360
Very cool.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:10.510
Hopefully you enjoyed that video.

